# Founder Scout — Sourcing Engine
## Find exceptional student builders before the company is obvious

Date: 18 September 2026

This document defines the sourcing system for Founder Scout.

Founder Scout is NOT a directory of everyone at a university.

It is a sourcing engine designed to discover unusually strong student and recent-graduate builders through observable evidence:

- things they built
- code they shipped
- hackathon projects
- research
- technical teams
- repeated collaboration
- product launches
- open-source work
- early startup formation
- momentum over time

The goal is:

> Find the person before the company is obvious.

---

# 1. CORE PRINCIPLE

Founder Scout should source broadly but promote selectively.

The pipeline is:

```text
Sources
↓
Raw people / projects
↓
Identity resolution
↓
Founder profiles
↓
Evidence aggregation
↓
Candidate promotion
↓
Founder Scout
↓
Shortlist

Do NOT deeply research every person discovered.

Most records should remain cheap, lightweight records.

Only increasingly interesting founders receive increasingly expensive enrichment.

